ntzenhofer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Dientzenhofer</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Dientzenhofer was a German Baroque architect from a Bavarian family of builders.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-friedrich-bottger"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-friedrich-bottger.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Friedrich Böttger</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Friedrich Böttger was a German alchemist held at the court of Augustus the Strong, who expected him to make gold.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-friedrich-struensee"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-friedrich-struensee.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Friedrich Struensee</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Friedrich Struensee was a German physician who became royal doctor to the mentally ill Christian VII of Denmark and the lover of Queen Caroline Matilda.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-froben"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-froben.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Froben</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Froben was a printer and publisher in Basel and one of the leading printers of the Renaissance.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-geiler-von-kaysersberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-geiler-von-kaysersberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Geiler von Kaysersberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Geiler von Kaysersberg was a priest and the most celebrated preacher of late medieval Germany, who held the pulpit of Strasbourg Cathedral from 1478 until his…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-georg-ii-fuchs-von-dornheim"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-georg-ii-fuchs-von-dornheim.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Georg II Fuchs von Dornheim</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Georg II Fuchs von Dornheim was prince-bishop of Bamberg from 1623 to 1633, known as the 'witch bishop'.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-gottfried-herder"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-gottfried-herder.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Gottfried Herder</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Gottfried Herder was a German philosopher, theologian and writer, born in Mohrungen in East Prussia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-gottlieb-christaller"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-gottlieb-christaller.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Gottlieb Christaller</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Gottlieb Christaller was a German missionary and linguist of the Basel Mission who worked on the Gold Coast, now Ghana, from 1853.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-heinrich-pestalozzi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-heinrich-pestalozzi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Heinrich Pestalozzi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Heinrich Pestalozzi was a Swiss educational reformer born in Zürich.</span></a></li><li class="enc-i